WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.665
shinjitai
I want to believe

00:03.765 --> 00:06.825
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light that I found that day

00:07.305 --> 00:09.995
kimi to kawashita
Because I still have

00:10.035 --> 00:14.705
tatta hitotsuno yakusoku ga arukara
That one promise that I made to you

00:15.115 --> 00:22.105
mou tachidomarazuni aruite yukitai
I want to keep walking, never stopping

00:23.815 --> 00:26.655
Dragon Drive

00:26.685 --> 00:32.215
uresugita kajitsu wo kajiru youni
Like biting into an overripe fruit

00:32.325 --> 00:35.265
yowai jibun ni
I was spoiling myself

00:35.295 --> 00:38.565
amaetsuzukete ita
I was giving in to my weakness

00:39.035 --> 00:43.365
kimi ni deawanakereba
If I hadn't met you

00:43.405 --> 00:45.335
ima mo
I'd still...

00:45.375 --> 00:51.715
kabe wo kowasu koto nado dekinakatta yo
...be unable to break the walls around me

00:53.415 --> 00:55.745
wasurenai
I'll never forget

00:55.785 --> 00:59.015
ano hi kanjita itami
The pain that I felt that day

00:59.325 --> 01:04.285
nido to ano basho modoritakunai
I never want to go back to that place

01:04.325 --> 01:05.915
motto tsuyoku
This strong feeling

01:06.025 --> 01:08.395
shinjitai
I want to believe

01:08.435 --> 01:11.595
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light I found that day

01:11.965 --> 01:16.995
kakkowarui to warawaretemo ii
Let them laugh and call me a loser

01:17.035 --> 01:19.735
bukiyou dakara
Because I'm clumsy

01:19.775 --> 01:27.475
onaji ikikata shika erabenainda
I can only choose to live life this way

01:47.635 --> 01:48.665
Kouhei!

01:55.415 --> 01:56.905
Too bad!

02:02.355 --> 02:04.645
Kouhei!

02:04.685 --> 02:05.585
This...

02:06.085 --> 02:07.575
...will finish you!

02:24.135 --> 02:26.005
It was just a dream.

02:27.045 --> 02:31.375
But it's no dream that Kouhei
has run off with the Dragonite!

02:33.745 --> 02:35.235
I cannot give up!

02:35.455 --> 02:36.745
Right, Chibi?!

02:38.685 --> 02:40.015
Chibi?

02:40.585 --> 02:41.575
Chibi!

02:41.955 --> 02:42.885
What's wrong?!

02:44.665 --> 02:47.895
Rebirth

02:50.395 --> 02:52.495
Elder. How is he?

02:53.165 --> 02:54.435
This is not good.

02:54.475 --> 02:55.935
What do you mean not good?!

02:56.035 --> 02:57.095
Can't he be saved?!

02:57.505 --> 02:59.475
I'm not certain of the cause...

02:59.905 --> 03:02.675
...but Senkohcoola's body temperature
is falling at an alarming rate.

03:03.475 --> 03:04.915
Unless we do something...

03:04.915 --> 03:06.645
...he could eventually die.

03:06.915 --> 03:08.435
This can't be happening!

03:08.615 --> 03:10.145
What am I to do?!

03:10.185 --> 03:11.775
There is a way to heal him.

03:11.855 --> 03:13.085
Wh-What is it?!

03:13.185 --> 03:14.315
Hurry up and tell me!

03:14.495 --> 03:17.055
I'm sure he'll get better,
if he can just get some outei.

03:17.355 --> 03:18.625
Outei?

03:19.165 --> 03:21.565
It's a precious medicinal herb...

03:21.765 --> 03:23.285
...found only atop the mountain east of here.

03:23.795 --> 03:26.565
It is known to effectively recover
a dragon's life force.

03:27.035 --> 03:28.405
If we have that...

03:28.435 --> 03:32.105
...at the least we can be assured
that Senkohcoola will live.

03:32.275 --> 03:33.965
Okay! I'll go and get some!

03:34.145 --> 03:35.075
Wait.

03:35.115 --> 03:36.575
Reaching the top of that mountain...

03:36.645 --> 03:38.845
...is not an easy feat!

03:39.045 --> 03:39.975
It's dangerous!

03:40.015 --> 03:41.485
We'll have someone else go.

03:41.555 --> 03:43.645
No, I'll go and get some myself!

03:44.315 --> 03:47.815
Up to now, I'm the one
who's always been helped by Chibi.

03:48.495 --> 03:51.685
So this time, I want to pay Chibi back!

03:52.365 --> 03:54.455
I wanna be the one to help Chibi.

03:56.495 --> 03:57.795
Wait here, Chibi.

03:57.835 --> 04:00.355
I'll be right back with those medicinal herbs!

04:01.435 --> 04:03.335
- Reiji!
- Wait a minute!

04:03.405 --> 04:04.875
Hey, don't go alone!

04:05.075 --> 04:06.065
Wait!

04:08.015 --> 04:09.135
There's something else...

04:09.175 --> 04:10.835
...that I'd like to ask your help with.

04:10.875 --> 04:12.145
Something else?

04:12.415 --> 04:15.505
But Kouhei's already gone to Earth
with the Dragonite.

04:15.655 --> 04:16.775
The battle's over!

04:16.915 --> 04:17.905
No.

04:18.185 --> 04:21.055
It's not over yet. We still have a chance.

04:32.235 --> 04:33.925
The output isn't stable yet!

04:36.935 --> 04:37.835
Dad!

04:37.875 --> 04:39.135
I did it!

04:39.245 --> 04:41.305
I got the last item!

04:43.445 --> 04:45.705
So this concludes everything, right?

04:50.315 --> 04:52.345
So that's the Dragonite.

04:52.825 --> 04:54.985
Dad! Say something!

04:55.195 --> 04:56.815
You're happy, aren't you?

04:58.665 --> 04:59.645
Why?

05:06.665 --> 05:08.895
Why did you return
in the middle of your mission?

05:09.035 --> 05:10.475
M-Middle?

05:10.935 --> 05:13.375
You've made the same mistake
that girl made.

05:13.775 --> 05:15.175
You fool.

05:15.415 --> 05:16.675
That girl?

05:20.685 --> 05:22.015
Return to Rikyu...

05:22.455 --> 05:24.045
...and carry out your mission.

05:25.455 --> 05:27.755
Wh... What are you saying, Dad?

05:27.885 --> 05:29.655
I returned with the Dragonite.

05:29.825 --> 05:31.125
Show me how this game ends.

05:31.695 --> 05:33.095
Please, Dad!

05:35.235 --> 05:36.855
That's not it!

05:38.265 --> 05:41.755
Shinryu cannot be revived
with that Dragonite!

05:42.175 --> 05:43.695
Wh-What do you mean?

05:44.745 --> 05:46.935
That's a key.

05:47.345 --> 05:48.575
A key?

05:48.715 --> 05:50.575
You're not making any sense to me.

05:51.045 --> 05:52.915
The Dragonite Kouhei took with him...

05:53.415 --> 05:55.445
...is not what Shinryu is sealed in.

05:57.915 --> 06:03.185
The Dragonite is a key to the Shrine
of the Four Holy Dragons.

06:07.625 --> 06:10.925
The Dragonite alone cannot revive Shinryu.

06:11.935 --> 06:14.495
Because that's nothing but a key.

06:16.275 --> 06:18.395
So you knew all along, Meguru.

06:18.805 --> 06:19.795
Yes.

06:20.075 --> 06:22.335
I see. That's why you...

06:23.415 --> 06:26.045
RI-ON will return to Rikyu once again...

06:26.145 --> 06:27.745
...to revive Shinryu.

06:28.315 --> 06:29.945
But with their present device...

06:30.085 --> 06:32.245
...it's hard to say when they'll be back.

06:32.955 --> 06:33.855
That's why...

06:33.885 --> 06:35.885
We need to hurry.

06:36.425 --> 06:38.555
We must win against them next time.

06:38.825 --> 06:40.885
Then why don't we begin training for it?

06:41.295 --> 06:42.265
First...

06:42.565 --> 06:44.865
...there's one thing I need you to investigate.

06:45.605 --> 06:47.795
I've heard that there are other people here.

06:47.835 --> 06:49.495
People from Earth...

06:49.535 --> 06:52.665
...besides us, and the guys from RI-ON.

07:12.895 --> 07:14.415
Sorry, Daisuke.

07:14.595 --> 07:15.725
You can go ahead.

07:15.765 --> 07:17.325
Kanper seems upset, for one thing.

07:17.365 --> 07:19.165
What?! What are you saying?

07:19.205 --> 07:20.725
We can't leave you behind!

07:24.235 --> 07:25.675
What do you think you're doing?!

07:28.875 --> 07:30.575
Hang in there, Chibi.

07:33.645 --> 07:35.045
You must be kidding!

07:39.825 --> 07:42.085
Chibi's waiting for me!

08:00.775 --> 08:02.865
This forest is kinda spooky.

08:03.275 --> 08:05.545
Are you sure we'll find people living here?

08:05.885 --> 08:08.405
Well, Meguru said we would.

08:09.385 --> 08:12.015
The other day, there was an incident...

08:12.255 --> 08:13.985
...where dragons living
in the western forest became violent.

08:14.225 --> 08:17.085
Then, someone appeared with his dragon...

08:17.255 --> 08:19.195
...and defeated those dragons in no time.

08:19.525 --> 08:21.515
According to someone
who witnessed the incident...

08:21.565 --> 08:23.295
...that person was likely from Earth.

08:23.865 --> 08:26.855
Should that person be
associated with RI-ON...

08:28.705 --> 08:30.605
What happens if that person
is associated with RI-ON?

08:30.635 --> 08:32.805
We'll simply get rid of such a person.

08:33.345 --> 08:35.135
It's only logical to get rid of potential foes...

08:35.315 --> 08:36.605
...before they get organized.

08:36.715 --> 08:37.705
Are you serious?!

08:37.745 --> 08:40.475
Listen, we've got our hands full
fighting Kouhei alone.

08:40.785 --> 08:43.545
Just think of what'll happen
if RI-ON adds to their battle force.

08:43.585 --> 08:45.075
You get it now?

08:45.325 --> 08:46.615
- Hey.
- What?

08:47.085 --> 08:48.525
What's this?

08:49.125 --> 08:51.685
This looks like the aftermath
of a dragon gone wild.

08:52.765 --> 08:55.885
Then could this be the battle
Meguru was talking about?

08:55.935 --> 08:56.695
No.

08:56.735 --> 08:59.665
This damage wasn't caused
by numerous dragons.

08:59.935 --> 09:01.925
This was caused by a single dragon.

09:01.975 --> 09:04.405
One very powerful dragon, that is.

09:05.645 --> 09:06.665
What's this?!

09:08.445 --> 09:09.965
This is too creepy!

09:10.015 --> 09:11.605
Wh-What is it with this forest?

09:12.085 --> 09:13.415
There's no mistake about it.

09:13.585 --> 09:15.375
There's something living in this forest.

09:18.725 --> 09:20.385
Wh-What's wrong?

09:45.285 --> 09:46.265
That's it!

09:52.685 --> 09:54.675
But the medicinal herb is within sight!

09:59.025 --> 10:00.155
Hang in there, Chibi!

10:23.855 --> 10:25.345
H-Hello!

10:25.755 --> 10:28.085
My name is Shirou Kurasawa!

10:28.125 --> 10:32.185
- Y-You're the one?
- Not a chance.

10:38.735 --> 10:39.855
Sorry to keep you waiting!

10:42.705 --> 10:44.005
Ow!

10:44.205 --> 10:46.005
- What do you think you're doing?!
- I'm so sorry!

10:46.045 --> 10:48.505
- I-I'll make another pot!
- Wait a second, mister!

10:48.815 --> 10:50.365
Never mind the tea.

10:50.715 --> 10:51.375
Huh?

10:51.415 --> 10:52.715
There's something we'd like to ask you.

10:52.945 --> 10:55.815
You're not from this world, are you?

10:56.315 --> 10:58.345
You're right, I'm not. Can you tell?

10:58.485 --> 11:00.755
- Then...
- Then you've been sent here by RI-ON!

11:01.025 --> 11:02.785
RI-ON? What's that?

11:02.855 --> 11:04.185
A new cuisine of some sort?

11:04.425 --> 11:05.685
This is no time for jokes!

11:05.725 --> 11:07.125
I've heard before...

11:07.165 --> 11:09.395
...although it's rare...

11:09.435 --> 11:12.095
...due to some effect, there are instances of
people being thrown from Earth to Rikyu.

11:12.365 --> 11:15.355
At any rate, this man appears
to have nothing to do with RI-ON.

11:15.605 --> 11:18.335
There's no way someone this dimwitted
could be working for RI-ON.

11:18.375 --> 11:19.365
You're right.

11:19.445 --> 11:22.275
By the way, don't you have
a partner dragon?

11:22.575 --> 11:25.135
P-Partner dragon?

11:27.785 --> 11:30.845
We came here upon hearing
that you defeated...

11:30.885 --> 11:32.715
...a number of violent dragons in this area!

11:32.785 --> 11:36.055
There's no way you could've done
such a thing without a partner dragon!

11:37.025 --> 11:39.185
I have no such thing!

11:39.225 --> 11:40.555
Y-You're lying!

11:40.595 --> 11:42.115
You really don't have one?

11:42.865 --> 11:44.425
I say there isn't, so there isn't.

11:44.465 --> 11:46.595
I don't like dragons in the first place.

11:51.005 --> 11:53.475
It's good that he's not affiliated with RI-ON.

11:53.605 --> 11:56.205
But he's not the one
who defeated all the dragons, either.

11:56.615 --> 11:59.075
Well, if he's got no dragon,
that would be impossible.

11:59.145 --> 12:03.175
But there can't be too many
people here from Earth.

12:07.925 --> 12:09.115
What's that?

12:14.795 --> 12:15.925
No mistake about it.

12:15.965 --> 12:17.955
There's a dragon trapped in here.

12:18.505 --> 12:22.125
Could it be the dragon
that became violent around here?

12:22.575 --> 12:23.695
You could be right.

12:23.735 --> 12:25.295
The dragon bones we saw...

12:25.345 --> 12:27.005
...could also be the work of the one in here.

12:27.045 --> 12:28.475
If we opened this, then...

12:28.515 --> 12:29.705
Bam!

12:29.745 --> 12:31.375
The dragon in here could go wild again!

12:32.715 --> 12:35.705
Well, our purpose here today
is not to pick a fight.

12:36.185 --> 12:37.705
Wh-Whaddaya say we leave?

12:37.755 --> 12:38.815
Let's leave.

12:50.995 --> 12:52.835
Chibi! Here are your medicinal herbs!

12:52.905 --> 12:54.765
You'll be feeling better in no time!

12:55.535 --> 12:56.505
Chibi?

12:56.535 --> 12:57.805
What's wrong? Hey.

12:58.005 --> 12:58.995
Chibi.

12:59.445 --> 13:00.845
Please, open your eyes.

13:00.875 --> 13:03.105
I brought you the medicinal herbs.

13:04.745 --> 13:07.145
Wake up, Chibi!

13:07.445 --> 13:10.215
Without you, I...

13:18.025 --> 13:19.015
Chibi!

13:24.265 --> 13:26.495
This is the violent dragon?

13:28.875 --> 13:30.895
But it's so gentle!

13:32.145 --> 13:34.305
Right. A bit different from our expectations.

13:34.445 --> 13:35.705
Not just a bit!

13:35.845 --> 13:38.215
- You talking back at me?!
- L-Look.

13:38.615 --> 13:39.735
That bandana's identical...

13:39.785 --> 13:42.515
...to the one in Shirou's room!

13:46.055 --> 13:47.355
Shirou!

13:48.695 --> 13:49.885
What is it?

13:50.855 --> 13:52.195
Do you still want to talk about something?

13:52.365 --> 13:54.195
You do have one!

13:54.295 --> 13:55.925
Why were you hiding the fact...

13:55.965 --> 13:58.125
...that you have a dragon partner?!

13:58.165 --> 14:00.795
Not only that, but
you've locked it up in a cave!

14:01.065 --> 14:02.665
I know nothing about such a dragon!

14:02.835 --> 14:04.635
I hate dragons!

14:04.875 --> 14:05.965
Bastard!

14:06.005 --> 14:07.305
How dare you feign ignorance?!

14:07.345 --> 14:08.405
Wait!

14:09.275 --> 14:12.405
This is the same as the one
that we saw in your home!

14:13.045 --> 14:14.985
You gave this to that dragon, right?

14:20.185 --> 14:23.715
Eager Striker was the first dragon I met...

14:23.755 --> 14:25.485
...when I came to this world.

14:48.985 --> 14:51.115
I got here without knowing how.

14:51.255 --> 14:54.715
Eager Striker was the first friend I had here.

14:55.725 --> 14:57.655
I was so happy...

14:58.055 --> 14:59.395
...back then.

15:00.025 --> 15:02.425
If he hadn't been by my side...

15:02.465 --> 15:04.225
...I'd probably be dead.

15:05.035 --> 15:06.765
Eager Striker was strong.

15:07.205 --> 15:08.895
That gave me assurance!

15:09.505 --> 15:10.435
I believed...

15:10.605 --> 15:12.575
...I believed that he was a true friend!

15:12.945 --> 15:13.935
But...

15:13.975 --> 15:15.705
...one day, suddenly...

15:16.945 --> 15:18.535
...he attacked me.

15:19.245 --> 15:20.905
Even though I trusted him.

15:24.455 --> 15:27.285
He... betrayed me.

15:29.055 --> 15:32.545
I will never see Eager Striker again.

15:32.825 --> 15:33.955
Don't say that.

15:38.935 --> 15:40.025
K-Kanper!

15:40.065 --> 15:41.625
What did you do that for?!

15:41.935 --> 15:43.425
What the hell's going on?

15:43.575 --> 15:44.625
It's the same!

15:44.905 --> 15:47.065
Just like when Eager Striker attacked me!

15:47.205 --> 15:48.765
Help me!

15:49.545 --> 15:51.605
This is why you can't trust dragons!

15:52.015 --> 15:54.845
These guys will never understand
how we feel!

15:55.115 --> 15:56.275
Get serious!

15:56.315 --> 15:59.085
Kanper and I have fought together
for a long time!

15:59.225 --> 16:00.945
There's no way he'd betray me!

16:06.125 --> 16:08.115
Huh? What's going on?

16:08.735 --> 16:10.225
What do you think you're doing, Kanper?

16:11.695 --> 16:12.755
Here's the cause.

16:13.305 --> 16:15.595
Kanper just saved your life.

16:16.735 --> 16:17.835
Wh-What's this?

16:18.105 --> 16:20.075
This kind of dragon
sucks blood from people.

16:20.745 --> 16:22.205
Don't be deceived by its small size.

16:22.245 --> 16:23.765
There's nothing cute about them.

16:24.075 --> 16:27.705
People have been known to die
from loss of blood because of them.

16:28.045 --> 16:29.035
Then...

16:29.115 --> 16:31.885
...it only looked like Kanper
attacked Daisuke because...

16:32.155 --> 16:33.275
I'm sure of it.

16:33.325 --> 16:35.415
Kanper was trying to protect
Daisuke from this one!

16:35.525 --> 16:37.115
Well, you should have said so!

16:38.125 --> 16:39.525
You're asking for too much.

16:39.565 --> 16:41.525
There aren't many dragons around
that can talk.

16:42.165 --> 16:43.595
- I got it!
- Huh?

16:43.895 --> 16:46.865
I'll bet that dragon was trying
to protect you as well!

16:47.035 --> 16:48.905
Think about it, you said yourself
what happened now...

16:48.935 --> 16:50.665
...was the same
as what happened with you!

16:50.775 --> 16:52.435
You'd better go over
and make up with that dragon!

16:52.675 --> 16:53.665
But...

16:53.905 --> 16:54.965
...I can't.

16:55.415 --> 16:57.675
I did something very cruel to Eager Striker.

16:57.815 --> 16:58.975
Unfortunately...

16:59.015 --> 17:01.415
...it seems we gotta take care of this first!

17:06.455 --> 17:08.045
Go, Kanper!

17:15.195 --> 17:16.725
There's no end to them!

17:16.965 --> 17:18.395
Hey, you help too!

17:19.365 --> 17:22.665
Come with your partner dragon
and fight with us!

17:22.775 --> 17:26.835
B-But, Eager Striker will never forgive me.

17:26.945 --> 17:29.375
This is no time for such talk! Look ahead!

17:29.875 --> 17:31.505
That's the leader of this group!

17:31.845 --> 17:32.935
Unless we defeat this one...

17:32.985 --> 17:35.005
...these guys will continue
attacking us forever!

17:35.115 --> 17:36.145
I...

17:36.555 --> 17:38.715
...I made a terrible mistake.

17:39.925 --> 17:41.015
Wh-What're you doing?!

17:41.055 --> 17:43.685
I'll lure these guys over to me!

17:43.755 --> 17:46.125
You defeat their leader
while they're distracted!

17:53.265 --> 17:54.235
That's him!

17:54.265 --> 17:55.895
But we can't get any closer.

17:56.005 --> 17:57.165
What are we to do?

18:04.415 --> 18:05.705
Eager Striker!

18:12.885 --> 18:14.685
Retreat for now! Otherwise they'll get you!

18:14.855 --> 18:17.455
It's all right. This is the way we fight!

18:18.495 --> 18:20.725
A bit more. A bit more.

18:22.195 --> 18:23.095
Now!

18:26.335 --> 18:27.525
A-Awesome.

18:27.965 --> 18:29.065
No, not yet!

18:45.215 --> 18:46.415
I-It can't be...

18:51.555 --> 18:52.785
- Why, that's!
- Reiji!

18:56.295 --> 18:58.495
Chibi looks different from usual.

18:58.765 --> 18:59.965
He's glowing.

19:00.435 --> 19:01.955
Here we go!

19:05.775 --> 19:06.575
Reiji!

19:06.575 --> 19:08.595
That dragon's an accumulation
of little dragons!

19:08.875 --> 19:10.575
You won't defeat them
by attacking them like that!

19:10.975 --> 19:13.415
Then why don't I get all of them at once?!

19:13.715 --> 19:16.015
Go!

19:28.625 --> 19:30.255
I see that Chibi has recovered!

19:30.395 --> 19:33.165
Yeah, although it wasn't
because of the medicinal herbs!

19:33.205 --> 19:35.765
Huh? Wasn't Chibi ill?

19:35.835 --> 19:37.395
Well, actually...

19:38.175 --> 19:39.465
Chibi!

19:42.415 --> 19:44.075
Chibi. What's happening to you?!

19:44.445 --> 19:45.635
Wh-Why...

19:45.685 --> 19:48.275
...Senkohcoola has matured.

19:48.485 --> 19:49.885
Matured?

19:50.355 --> 19:51.875
No mistake about it.

19:52.185 --> 19:54.515
I had heard a legend about this.

19:55.185 --> 19:56.625
Among the dragons is a type of dragon...

19:56.655 --> 20:00.685
...that matures after a number of battles...

20:00.725 --> 20:02.495
...to better maximize its abilities.

20:03.435 --> 20:05.595
They appear to die for a moment...

20:05.665 --> 20:08.535
...as they store all their power...

20:08.635 --> 20:10.225
...and then release it at once.

20:10.575 --> 20:13.595
I don't know if the legend is true...

20:13.745 --> 20:17.875
...for I have never encountered
such a dragon before.

20:18.075 --> 20:20.205
So Chibi's one of those dragons?

20:21.945 --> 20:25.515
And then I came here
because I was worried about you guys!

20:26.725 --> 20:29.655
Well, I guess that dragon's
not called Rikyu's savior for nothing.

20:29.895 --> 20:31.955
In any case, I'm so glad to see Chibi's okay.

20:34.165 --> 20:35.155
Okay!

20:36.865 --> 20:38.995
Thank you, Eager Striker.

20:39.435 --> 20:41.735
You guys are strong.

20:41.835 --> 20:43.235
Yeah, you were a great help.

20:45.105 --> 20:48.565
Um, Shirou, would you be interested
in joining us...

20:48.775 --> 20:49.745
I'm sorry.

20:49.775 --> 20:52.875
I'd rather remain alone
with this guy for now.

20:53.115 --> 20:54.605
What? But why?

20:54.685 --> 20:57.375
I assumed I knew everything about him...

20:57.615 --> 20:59.245
...when in fact I knew nothing.

20:59.525 --> 21:02.315
So I wanna become better friends with him.

21:03.255 --> 21:05.485
I must become a man worthy...

21:05.525 --> 21:08.015
...of a dragon who will come
and save me when I'm in trouble.

21:08.465 --> 21:10.555
That's more important to me.

21:10.695 --> 21:11.895
I'm sorry.

21:12.305 --> 21:13.965
There's nothing to apologize for.

21:14.035 --> 21:15.095
Do as you wish.

21:15.135 --> 21:16.125
Rockaku?

21:16.875 --> 21:19.895
He's neither our ally,
nor a member of RI-ON.

21:20.045 --> 21:21.265
Let's leave it at that!

21:21.305 --> 21:22.975
Uh-huh! You're right!

21:25.985 --> 21:27.245
They've returned!

21:27.315 --> 21:28.505
Good.

21:29.315 --> 21:31.215
What a relief, Chibi.

21:34.155 --> 21:36.355
I'll continue counting on you, Chibi.

21:37.495 --> 21:40.655
Because we'll be together forever, right?

21:55.975 --> 21:58.715
taikutsu datta
I was bored

21:58.715 --> 22:01.485
okubyou datta
I was a coward

22:01.485 --> 22:05.445
dareka wo jibun wo kizutsukete ita
I was hurting someone and myself

22:06.885 --> 22:09.655
tsuyogari itte
I tried to hide my weakness

22:09.655 --> 22:11.855
wagamama itte
I was being selfish

22:12.295 --> 22:16.425
doushiyoumonai kimochi mamoritsuzukete
Protecting the uncontrollable feeling

22:17.835 --> 22:20.505
otona ni natte
I became an adult

22:20.505 --> 22:23.235
kimi to deatte
Then I met you

22:23.235 --> 22:27.235
mune no sumikko yawarakaku natte
My heart got softened

22:28.545 --> 22:31.045
setsunaku natta
Longing for love

22:31.045 --> 22:34.045
dakishime atta
We embraced each other

22:34.045 --> 22:38.955
hakkiri mamorubeki mono wo mitsuketa
I finally knew what I wanted to protect

22:39.585 --> 22:42.325
tatta hitotsu no yuuki ga
Only one courage

22:42.325 --> 22:45.095
tatta hitotsu no kotoba ga
Just one word

22:45.095 --> 22:49.755
futari owaranai yume e to hakobu
Take us to an endless dream

22:50.465 --> 22:53.235
hon no chiisana yasashisa ga
Only a small kindness

22:53.235 --> 22:55.905
hon no wazuka na sasayaki ga
Only a small whisper

22:55.905 --> 23:00.565
futari wo sotto tsutsunde kureru
Wrap us gently

23:01.205 --> 23:05.735
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:06.645 --> 23:12.345
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:14.485 --> 23:17.395
Next time

23:17.395 --> 23:20.055
What?! We're still not strong enough
to beat Kouhei Toki?!

23:20.095 --> 23:22.225
- Trouble!
- Then why don't you...

23:22.465 --> 23:24.655
...increase your power?! Go ahead, Chibi!

23:25.495 --> 23:26.365
What's wrong?

23:26.405 --> 23:29.095
I'm suggesting that you "Poof" or "Bam"!

23:29.135 --> 23:31.265
And turn into something
more handsome and powerful!

23:31.305 --> 23:32.745
Poof! Bam!

23:32.745 --> 23:34.365
But you're still the same.

23:34.405 --> 23:35.605
Impossible!

23:35.645 --> 23:38.515
Next, on Dragon Drive,
"Rites of Passage".

23:38.815 --> 23:41.515
Okay, we're going on a journey
to train to become a warrior!

23:41.515 --> 23:41.785
Rites of Passage
Okay, we're going on a journey
to train to become a warrior!

23:41.785 --> 23:42.015
Rites of Passage

23:42.015 --> 23:44.385
Rites of Passage
Jab! Punch!
